                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Fair play to the developer for what I can say is a unique mechanic in a world flooded with Puyo / Tetris / Match 3 Clones, but this needs a little more polish to really be more fun. As it is, there's a barrage of colours and sounds that are relentless as you play, and it's highly distracting.\n\nThe mechanic of the game means that games do not last very long at all, and would almost be served better I believe if breakers were compulsory blocks given to the player - rather than the choosing option.\n\nIt's also totally okay to explain to the player how to play. I was incredibly irritated by the condescending star creature after blundering through the first level, and being told I finally 'got it'. I GOT NOTHING. \n\nCursed little twee chew toy. ୧༼ಠ益ರೃ༽୨",
